# Allow-list: the build context holds only what the Dockerfile copies.
# Everything else (.git, .venv, tests, docs, .claude, .github, infra, charts, monitoring,
# .env files, caches) never reaches the Docker daemon, so it cannot leak into a layer.
# Only Python source is allowed under app/, so a stray app/.env or key file can't be copied in.
*

!app/**/*.py
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock

# Re-exclude local bytecode inside the allowed paths.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
